Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 13 — Android Game Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand Android games regardless of the underlying engine. While engine-specific methodologies (Unity, Unreal, native engines, etc.) explain individual technologies, this section focuses on the architecture common to most games: gameplay systems, world simulation, rendering, input, persistence, networking, and performance. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct a game's complete design and execution model.



> Core Principle:
Games are real-time simulation systems. Recover the simulation first, then the supporting systems.




