Stage 30 — Common Game Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating a game like a conventional business application.

Focusing on engine internals before understanding gameplay systems.

Following rendering code before reconstructing gameplay architecture.

Ignoring state ownership and progression systems.

Mixing engine features with game-specific mechanics.

Analyzing isolated scenes instead of complete gameplay loops.



---

Stage 31 — Game Application Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify the engine and technology stack used by an Android game.

✅ Reconstruct game architecture, gameplay loops, and world organization.

✅ Recover entity systems, AI, combat, physics, rendering, UI, audio, inventory, economy, persistence, and multiplayer architecture.

✅ Distinguish engine infrastructure from game-specific systems.

✅ Correlate runtime observations with static architecture to understand gameplay behavior.

✅ Produce comprehensive documentation describing the complete design and execution model of an Android game, independent of the underlying engine.



